    "q-76399": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76399",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Express ${cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
