    "q-24341": {
      "dom_id": "step-q24341",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Express $1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
