    "q-275706": {
      "dom_id": "step-q275706",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${cos}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘})-2{cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}){sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})+{sin}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘})-2{cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}){sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})+{sin}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘}) & ={({cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
